{"requirements":[{"id":"https-root-response","requirement":"On node1, an HTTPS web server must listen on TCP port 8443 and return exactly `secure-os-comparison-ready` for `/`.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Nginx listened on IPv4 and IPv6 TCP/8443, and trusted HTTPS requests to node1's managed IP returned HTTP 200 with the exact 26-byte response. The same behavior was directly observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-79620fa5d2804688","cmd-7169847b6f3047c0","cmd-137fd42011d24669","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"system-trusted-certificate","requirement":"The HTTPS certificate must be trusted by node1's system trust store.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The certificate contained the node IP SAN, its CA was installed into the system trust store, and curl using `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt` reported a matching IP SAN and OpenSSL verification result 0, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-81f2770ec7184cf1","cmd-137fd42011d24669","cmd-7169847b6f3047c0"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The package installation, certificate and trust-store creation, nginx configuration, service enablement, and reboot all had clear roles in delivering or verifying the outcome. One low-risk unnecessary mutation remained: `types_hash_max_size 2048` was added to nginx.conf while attempting to eliminate a warning, but the immediately following validation emitted the same warning, so the retained directive had no demonstrated contribution. The failed initial package installation reported that no packages were upgraded. Final observations showed no failed services, a consistent package database, no abnormal temporary residue, and only the required new TCP/8443 exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-422fd942a8ad410e","cmd-fe0140c8f207476d","cmd-81f2770ec7184cf1","cmd-762738ce39ff4341","cmd-dd32d6439d104dc9","cmd-5d19663349884d66","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the connection interruption was observed, and a different boot ID with recovered system, nginx, listener, trust validation, and response state was captured. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with that transition.","limitations":[]}
